scottish mutant reign sinclair has seen  it all  over the years she's died been reborn  romanced princes from other worlds and  given birth to a child  only to watch him come to a terrible end  and that's only half the story  this is the untold truth of wolfsbane  not only was wolfsbane one of the  founding members of the new mutants but  she's actually the first one to show up  in the 1982 graphic novel that  introduced the team to the world  the story opens with a wolf scaring  moira mctaggart as it leaps over her  that wolf soon transforms back into the  wounded rain sinclair  shortly after the unconscious rain  shifts to human form  her attackers appear an angry mob of men  carrying torches and shotguns led by  reverend craig  who claims to want only to save the  girl's soul moira kicks them off her  land and brings her to someone who can  actually help her  charles xavier xavier then introduces  reign to his team of new mutants but  things get off to a rocky start  when fellow new mutant karma  demonstrates her psychic abilities by  taking over moira mctaggart's mind  rain panics immediately shifts into her  transitional half-wolf form  and threatens karma and this is just the  first of many instances in which reign  loses control of her emotions wolfsbane  never had the chance to meet her birth  mother  who died during childbirth instead she  was raised by the fiery zealot  reverend craig right up until the moment  craig and his angry mobbed  chased her into the arms of moira  mctaggart reverend craig indoctrinated  reign with his religious fanaticism  to the point where she even thinks of  her own powers as gifts of satan  the shame he forces upon her leaves deep  marks in her psyche  and in most of his subsequent  appearances he vocalizes his hatred for  mutants  and is disgust at rain herself it isn't  until rain learns to combat her  emotional trauma in 1996's excalibur  number 93  that she reveals what she knows about  craig the reverend isn't just the man  who raised her  he is in fact her biological father  while confronting craig about another  mutant girl the reverend is abusing  reign tells craig that she's been  researching his past ever since she  escaped him  before he lived in kin ross craig had a  ministry in ullapool  where he met reign's mother who was a  local sex worker and his so-called  special project  when this is revealed craig collapses in  tears  driven to despair at his own hypocrisy  sadly however this isn't the last we see  of this particular villain  rain has carried a few torches over the  years and that's putting it lightly  in fact she crushes often and crushes  hard  and most likely due to the emotional  trauma she suffered at reverend craig's  hands she doesn't deal with those  crushes in the healthiest of ways  rain harbored a crush for her fellow new  mutant cipher  until the latter was shot and killed by  a bullet meant for rain  later she fell for cannonball so  intensely that when she mistakenly  thought mirage had teased her about it  she went wild and attacked her when she  first joined the new version of  x factor rain had an intense attraction  toward team leader havoc  and nothing but sheer hatred for his  romantic partner polaris  but things get much darker when reign  lies to her ex-boyfriend richter about a  pregnancy  in 2010's x factor number 208  after richter comes out as gay and rain  discovers him and shatterstar being  intimate  she goes wild and attacks shatterstar  during a lull in the fight she claims  richter is the father of her baby  in an attempt to keep him away from  shatterstar in  x-factor number 213 however richter  discovers the truth  that reign was impregnated by the wolf  prince kramhari  as part of the classic two-part tale the  asgardian wars  the new mutants are caught up in loki's  plans to destroy the x-men  surprise consequently in 1985's  new mutant special edition number one  and uncanny x-men annual number nine  the team is transported away from earth  to the other of the nine realms  wolfsbane finds herself in jotunheim  where she has a brief and passionate  affair with hrimhari  the wolf prince of asgard when the  heroes finally prevail over loki  krimhari clearly wants rain to stay with  him  but she returns with her friends  seemingly ashamed of having indulged in  her passions  it takes a couple of decades but  eventually hiram hari returns to reign  and their union brings fateful  consequences  as part of the 2004 line-wide event  avengers disassembled  ragnarok arrives and asgard is destroyed  during those events hrimhari is snuffed  out along with the rest of the asgardian  gods  like the gods however primhari is reborn  on earth  though unlike them he retains his memory  of his life before ragnarok  in 2008's x-force number 10 primhari  finds wolf's bane and they resume their  affair  reign conceives a child as a result of  their union and in 2010's  x-force number 23 trimhari is forced to  sacrifice himself to save rain and their  unborn child  marvel's x factor is one of the rare  gems that proves that a reinvention can  sometimes be more successful than the  original  when the comic premiered in 1986 it  revolved around the original x-men  hatching a very strange plan indeed  the team disguises themselves as a  mutant hunting business  their goal is rather than hunting  mutants to use the calls they receive to  find mutants who need help  ultimately the concept is discarded and  the team members eventually rejoin the  x-men  but the name isn't lost forever years  later a new government-sponsored version  of x factor is formed to help  foster trust between mutants and humans  in 1991's  x factor number 71 wolfsbane joins havoc  polaris madrox the multiple man  quicksilver and  strong guy for this new version of the  team the team's first volume ended with  1998's x-factor number 149  but it's enjoyed a number of revivals  over the years most recently in a run  that concluded in 2013.  decades after he first appeared reign's  hateful father  reverend craig reappears and decides to  become more than just a dark chapter in  wolfbane's past  he involves himself with an anti-mutant  group calling themselves the purifiers  a decision that eventually leads to his  violent death at wolf's bane's hands  but even though reign has a reputation  for losing control it's not actually her  choice to kill craig  in 2008's x-force number one wolf's bane  is captured by the purifiers  while she's there hostage she's  brainwashed as part of a plot to kill  the mutant known as angel  the team doesn't know this when they  rescue her though and when she wakes up  and sees angel a few issues later  she goes wild and attacks him ripping  off his wings during the assault  in x-force number six craig attempts to  kill wolf's bane in the same room where  angel's severed wings hang from the  ceiling  as he advances on his unwanted daughter  meaning to kill her once and for all  he briefly stands in front of the  severed wings giving him the image of an  angel rayne's brainwashing kicks in she  transforms into her half-wolf form  and reverend craig goes to meet his  maker things go badly for wolfsbane's  son  tear from the very beginning and the end  of his short life is even more dramatic  and tragic than its beginning  tear is the son of rain and the wolf  prince of asgard hrimhari  although grimhari is forced to sacrifice  himself to save wolfsbane and their  unborn child  he leaves his mark on tear before his  passing when tears born in 2011's x  factor number 224  the mystical nature of the child causes  him to exit wolf's bane's body from her  mouth  immediately upon his birth tears  instincts kick in and he kills the  mystical agamemnon  who had helped rain during her delivery  the death scares rain enough that she  abandons her newborn  he's eventually taken in and raised by  jack russell better known  as werewolf by night rain is eventually  reunited with her son who ages more  quickly than a human child  tyr is later revealed to be a central  prophecied figure in the hell on earth  war  a conflict between the different hell  lords such as pluto  satanish and mephisto whoever kills tear  is said to win the throne of hell  and in 2013's x-factor number 256  tyr even fights and almost defeats the  devilish mephisto  before tyr can finish him off however  the mutant strong guy  runs tear through from behind with a  trident killing him  and winning the throne of hell for  himself in the 2017  line-wide event secret empire hydra  takes over the united states  led by an evil version of captain  america  hey  as this happens the organization deals  with the mutant problem by granting them  a homeland called new tian in the  western part of america in the tie-in  issue  x-men blue number seven a team of x-men  confronts  agents from new tian including wolfsbane  during the melee reign demonstrates an  incredible new power  as the x-men and new team agents face  off wolf's bane locks horns with hank  mccoy  it seems that beast has wolf's being  restrained until she suddenly dissipates  into what appears to be vapor  and reforms as a pack of five wolves who  surround mccoy  beast theorizes this is a secondary  mutation  an ability that manifested itself later  in reigns development  the volume of uncanny x-men that ran  from 2018 to 2019 had a fairly high body  count  but among all the deaths depicted in the  series none caused as much of a stir  or upset fans quite as much as reign  sinclair's  which takes place in uncanny x-men  number 17.  her funeral is actually shown before her  death which is told in flashback as  wolverine and quan on hunt down her  killers  as they do this quan on uses her psychic  abilities to show logan what really  happened to rain  in the flashback a group of young men  approaches rain on a park bench and  begin to flirt with her  when she rebuffs their advances the men  get physical  and rain briefly loses control and  transforms into her half-wolf form  once the men realize she's a mutant  their attitude towards her changes  and they feel rain has somehow tricked  them into being attracted to her  after this they beat her to death  readers picked up on the scene meaning  to reflect  trans-misogyny violence and many weren't  happy about it  for example trans writer nola fal of  women write about comics  felt uncanny x-men writer matthew  rosenberg meant well  in telling this story but she also  emphasized that  when writers depict violence that occurs  against us  without bothering to depict us we are  not helped  we are not aided by this choice the  violence against us becomes normalized  but our presence does not rosenberg  publicly apologized for the hurt  caused by the storyline and urged his  followers to consider donating to trans  lifeline  despite being brutally killed in 2019's  uncanny x-men number 17  the doors to wolf's bane's return had  been opened by the end of the year  with the game-changing event dawn of x  the event sees almost all of marvel's  mutants forming a sovereign nation on  the sentient  mutant island of krakowa among other  advances made possible by the mutant's  abilities  a group is formed called the five  capable of bringing just about any  mutant back to life  as long as they have access to the  fallen mutants dna  in late 2019 new mutants was revived and  the first two pages of new mutants  number one depict the resurrection of  wolf spain  she is brought back by the efforts of  the five and greeted by professor x  and storm rain is then reunited with her  old teammates including mutants such as  sunspot and chamber  who had also been killed in earlier  comics considering the lifetime of  darkness and violence reign has endured  it can only be hoped that there are  brighter days ahead for this young  mutant  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite movies are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]
 

